Without the /v flag, regular expressions are not "Unicode-aware".

The (?flag) syntax is a group modifier (inline flag modifier).

It allows for modifying flags in a part of a pattern, rather than to the entire pattern.

(?flags:pattern) enables the flags only for the pattern in the group.

ThedotAllproperty returnstrueif the /s flag is set.

Theglobalproperty returnstrueif the /g flag is set.

ThehasIndicesproperty returnstrueif the /d flag is set.

TheignoreCaseproperty returnstrueif the /i flag is set.

Themultilineproperty returnstrueif the /m flag is set.

Thestickyproperty returnstrueif the /y flag is set.

Theunicodeproperty returnstrueif the /u flag is set.

TheunicodeSetsproperty returnstrueif the /v flag is set.

